            "review_comment": [
                "```suggestion\r\n\t\t\tmap.from(properties.getConjurUrl()).whenNonNull().to(configuration::conjurUrl);\r\n```",
                "The method reference does not work when executing against the 5.x/6.x older `FluentConfiguration` which does not have the `conjur**` or `vault**` mutators. Regardless of the value being null, at runtime the method reference still attempts to get resolved at which time a NoSuchMethod gets thrown. This is why the file is littered w/ comments like this ```No method reference for compatibility with Flyway 6.x```. \r\n\r\nTo see this in action run `org.springframework.boot.autoconfigure.flyway.Flyway5xAutoConfigurationTests` or `org.springframework.boot.autoconfigure.flyway.Flyway6xAutoConfigurationTests`. "
            ],
